{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"debug":1},true],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"slug":1,"metadata":2,"images":124,"html":271,"xml":325},"ISic000762",{"file":1,"uri":1,"title":3,"status":4,"editions":6,"editionAuthor":19,"type":20,"support":25,"objectType":26,"material":30,"condition":38,"dimensions":40,"layoutDesc":51,"handNote":60,"date":92,"places":97,"geo":107,"country":102,"provenance":99,"provenanceFound":111,"provenanceGeo":117,"provenanceObserved":118,"provenanceLost":19,"graphics":124,"region":134,"settlement":135,"repository":136,"textLang":152,"bibliographyEdition":156,"bibliographyDiscussion":204,"citation":207,"tmNumber":8,"facsimile":234,"letterHeights":235,"publications":250,"zotero":255,"keywords":260},"Part of a base for a dedication(?)",{"_":5},"edited",[7,10,12,14,17],{"_":8,"type":9},"175798","TM",{"type":11},"EDR",{"type":13},"EDH",{"_":15,"type":16},"6100291","EDCS",{"type":18},"PHI",null,{"_":21,"ana":22,"ref":23,"cert":24},"dedication","#function.dedication","https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription/Dedication","low","A large grey limestone block, the front face of which angles in towards the base. Broken at the left end, intact above, below and to the right. The rear right corner has been cut away, and there is a recessed clamp hole on the upper face towards the rear right corner. Roughly finished on all sides except the front face. ",{"_":27,"ana":28,"ref":29},"block","#object.block","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/189.html",{"_":31,"ana":32,"type":33,"subtype":34,"resp":36,"ref":37},"limestone","#material.inorganic.stone.sedimentary_rock.limestone.calcite_limestone.grey","stone.limestone.polishable.grey",[35],"unspecified","#Coccato","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/66.html",{"ana":39},"#condition.damaged",[41,45,48],{"_":42,"unit":43,"dimension":44},"28.2-28.8","cm","height",{"_":46,"unit":43,"dimension":47},"64.5-72","width",{"_":49,"unit":43,"dimension":50},"33-37.3","depth",{"layout":52},{"p":53,"rs":54,"damage":58},"The right end of three lines of Latin letters, seemingly originally cnetred on the stone, given the large vacats to the end of lines 1 and 3. The stone increasingly damaged to the left edge of the face. Hederae at the end of each line.",{"_":55,"ana":56,"ref":57},"chiselled","#execution.chiselled","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1",{"ana":59},"#text_condition.incomplete",{"lettering":61,"dimensions":62},"Deeply v-cut letters, tending to the tall and narrow, with basic wedge seerifs at the end of strokes; some letters lean to the left, R has an extended tail, A and M slightly extended upwards beyond the apex.",[63,71,77,83,89],{"type":64,"l":65,"from":66,"to":66,"h":67,"unit":68,"atLeast":69,"atMost":70},"letterHeight","Line 1","line1","53-60","mm","53","60",{"type":64,"l":72,"from":73,"to":73,"h":74,"unit":68,"atLeast":75,"atMost":76},"Line 2","line2","40-54","40","54",{"type":64,"l":78,"from":79,"to":79,"h":80,"unit":68,"atLeast":81,"atMost":82},"Line 3","line3","35-45","35","45",{"type":84,"l":85,"from":66,"to":73,"h":86,"unit":68,"atLeast":87,"atMost":88},"interlinear","Interlineation line 1 to 2","20-23","20","23",{"type":84,"l":90,"from":73,"to":79,"h":91,"unit":68,"atLeast":91,"atMost":91},"Interlineation line 2 to 3","25",{"_":93,"notBefore":94,"notAfter":95,"evidence":96},"Imperial; form of M implies 2nd century or later",101,300,"lettering",[98,103],{"_":99,"type":100,"ref":101,"region":102},"Cosconiana","ancient","https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462166","Sicilia",{"_":104,"type":105,"ref":106,"region":102},"Canicatti","modern","https://www.geonames.org/2525405",[108],[109,110],37.355098,13.8056491,{"_":112,"type":113,"subtype":114,"geo":115,"geoCert":116},"Found c.1972 in a late antique wall in contrada Vito Soldano, c.4km west of Canicatti, area of a late Roman settlement commonly identified with Cosconiana (not Agrigento, contra Manganaro 1989); now on display in Agrigento Archaeological Museum.","fo